      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The consequences of coital experience in the non-pregnant female are varied and are occasional diagnostic puzzles. They range from those typified by manifest or concealed haemorrhage, to those revealed by immunologic, neurologic or pharmacologic phenomena and to those, whose patho-physiology is as yet, unclear. Observations are made of the likelihood of recurrence, and that, most patients would typically not readily admit to the preceding act of coitus."},
